---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CountUp from "../components/motion/CountUp.astro";
import SimpleHero from "../components/hero/SimpleHero.astro";
import { Picture } from "astro:assets";
import CTASection from "../components/sections/CTASection.astro";
import { offer } from "../data/school";
import { business, cityState, founded, team } from "../data/business";
import { ratingText } from "../data/reviews";

import michaelTeaching from "../images/our-story/founder-michael-lowery-teaching-class.jpg";
import michaelPortrait from "../images/our-story/founder-michael-lowery-smiling-in-dojo.jpg";
import studentActionShot from "../images/our-story/students-kicking-pad-drill-raeford-dojo.jpg";
import beltsAfterTest from "../images/our-story/students-new-belts-after-rank-test.jpg";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Our Story"
  fullTitle="Our Story | Action Zone CMA | Martial Arts in Raeford, NC"
  description={`${business.displayName} has taught Yeshua's Ryu since ${founded.year}. The story of founder ${team.founder.name} and the school he built.`}
  path="/our-story"
  ogImage={michaelTeaching}
  ogImageAlt={`Founder ${team.founder.name} teaching a martial arts class on the mat`}
>
  <SimpleHero eyebrow="Our Story">
    <Fragment slot="heading">Since {founded.year}. <em>One standard.</em></Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="subtext">
      Action Zone was not built to be the biggest school in the area. It was built to change who
      walks out the door.
    </Fragment>
  </SimpleHero>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-20 md:pt-16 md:px-5">
    <h2 class="mb-5 text-[clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.2rem)] text-indigo">It didn't start in a dojo.</h2>
    <div class="text-lg leading-loose text-[#40403A] md:leading-normal">
      <p class="mb-6 md:mb-4">
        At eight years old, Michael Lowery was attacked and robbed outside his family's business at Washington, D.C.'s Union Market. Soon after, a man who did business with his father began teaching him martial arts on a basketball court across the street. Michael was hooked. He studied every move he could find, even the ones on TV in <em>The Wild Wild West</em>, <em>Kung Fu</em>, and <em>The Green Hornet</em>, and practiced them with joy.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-14 md:pt-12 md:px-5">
    <h2 class="mb-5 text-[clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.2rem)] text-indigo">Hard years. Real lessons.</h2>
    <div class="text-lg leading-loose text-[#40403A] md:leading-normal">
      <p class="mb-6 md:mb-4">
        Michael is a member of the Lumbee Tribe, from a line of warriors that includes the legendary Henry Berry Lowry. He grew up in Wagram and Fayetteville, North Carolina, through the racial unrest of the '60s and '70s, and spent summers at the family business in D.C., some of them living in an old World War II army bus with no heat or running water. His real-world training came on Hay Street, Fort Bragg Road, and Bragg Boulevard, often against soldiers home from Vietnam. He worked as an iron worker and welder in rough places, and by his own account, he didn't always make the right choices.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-14 md:pt-12 md:px-5">
    <h2 class="mb-5 text-[clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.2rem)] text-indigo">Then he met Jesus.</h2>
    <div class="text-lg leading-loose text-[#40403A] md:leading-normal">
      <p class="mb-6 md:mb-4">
        In 1983, a radical encounter with Jesus changed everything. Michael began attending Manna Church, served in youth ministry for two years, and was blessed to sit under the teaching of Michael Fletcher. A couple of years later, he stepped into his first commercial dojo.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-14 md:pt-12 md:px-5">
    <h2 class="mb-5 text-[clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.2rem)] text-indigo">Faith and art, together.</h2>
    <div class="text-lg leading-loose text-[#40403A] md:leading-normal">
      <p class="mb-6 md:mb-4">
        At 28, one of his teachers, Master Jung, invited him to Korea to study combat taekwondo and Buddhism. Michael said no. He had to work, and he had his own faith: he was "a Jesus person." Master Jung's answer stayed with him: then couple your faith with your art. That became Yeshua's Ryu, "Jesus' Way." It's a kinder approach that blends the arts Michael mastered as praise to God's grace, love, forgiveness, and mercies that are new every morning.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-16 bg-indigo py-20 text-white md:mt-14 md:py-18">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-4xl gap-8 px-6 md:px-5 sm:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] sm:items-center">
      <div class="mx-auto h-40 w-40 overflow-hidden rounded-full">
        <Picture
          src={michaelPortrait}
          alt={`Founder ${team.founder.name} smiling in the dojo`}
          formats={["avif", "webp"]}
          widths={[160, 320]}
          sizes="160px"
          pictureAttributes={{ class: "block h-full w-full" }}
          class="h-full w-full object-cover"
          style="object-position:50% 40%"
        />
      </div>
      <blockquote class="text-lg italic leading-relaxed text-[#E8E7F0]">
        <p class="mb-6 md:mb-4">
          "Our focus isn't on winning trophies or gaining recognition. Instead, we seek
          self-enlightenment and a deeper spiritual understanding through the demanding practice of
          martial arts."
        </p>
        <p>"Knowledge is incomplete without wisdom, and our habits define who we become."</p>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-14 md:pt-12 md:px-5">
    <h2 class="mb-5 text-[clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.2rem)] text-indigo">More than 35 years of teaching.</h2>
    <div class="text-lg leading-loose text-[#40403A] md:leading-normal">
      <p class="mb-6 md:mb-4">
        Since then, Michael has trained law enforcement officers, Fort Bragg soldiers and their spouses, prison officers, pastors, security professionals, and countless men, women, and children. He opened Action Zone in 1993 in Wilmington, moved to Good Middling Dr in Fayetteville, and eventually to Raeford, into the building he built himself.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <figure class="px-6 pt-14 md:px-5 md:pt-12">
    <div class="mx-auto aspect-square max-w-lg overflow-hidden rounded">
      <Picture
        src={michaelTeaching}
        alt={`Founder ${team.founder.name} teaching a class on the mat`}
        formats={["avif", "webp"]}
        widths={[420, 512, 768, 1024]}
        sizes="(min-width: 512px) 512px, 100vw"
        pictureAttributes={{ class: "block h-full w-full" }}
        class="h-full w-full object-cover"
        style="object-position:50% 6%"
      />
    </div>
    <figcaption class="mt-3 text-center text-sm font-semibold text-mist">{team.founder.honorific} {team.founder.name}, founder</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-14 md:pt-12 md:px-5">
    <h2 class="mb-5 text-[clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.2rem)] text-indigo">A family legacy.</h2>
    <div class="text-lg leading-loose text-[#40403A] md:leading-normal">
      <p class="mb-6 md:mb-4">
        Today Michael is semi-retired, but he still oversees the family dojo. His son Jayson Lindemuth and daughter Hannah carry his legacy forward, fully intact. More than anything, Michael loves Jesus, and he especially loves kids.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 md:px-5">
    <div class="py-20 text-lg leading-loose text-[#40403A] md:py-16 md:leading-normal">
      <p class="mb-6 md:mb-4">
        What he built was not a franchise or a fitness trend. Yeshua's Ryu is his own system,
        drawn from more than fifty years in the art, blending Karate, Jiu Jitsu, Kung Fu, Tae Kwon
        Do, and the five traditional Japanese weapons into one thing that gets taught the same way
        every night.
      </p>
      <p>We are a non-competitive school. That is on purpose, and Michael has always been direct about why.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 md:px-5">
    <p class="py-20 text-lg leading-loose text-[#40403A] md:py-16 md:leading-normal">
      That standard shows up in who is allowed to teach here. Every instructor has put in a
      minimum of 480 hours to earn their Black Belt, plus a leadership program on top of it. Your
      child is not being handed off to someone who learned the moves last year.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="bg-paper-warm py-18 md:py-14">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-3xl grid-cols-3 gap-6 px-6 md:px-5 text-center">
      <div>
        <div class="font-display text-3xl font-black text-indigo">{founded.year}</div>
        <div class="mt-1 text-sm text-mist">Teaching since</div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="font-display text-3xl font-black text-indigo"><CountUp value="480" />+</div>
        <div class="mt-1 text-sm text-mist">Hours to Black Belt</div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="font-display text-3xl font-black text-indigo"><CountUp value={ratingText} /></div>
        <div class="mt-1 text-sm text-mist">Google rating</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl grid-cols-1 gap-6 px-6 md:px-5 py-20 sm:grid-cols-2 md:py-16">
    <div class="aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden rounded">
      <Picture
        src={studentActionShot}
        alt="Students mid-technique during a training session"
        formats={["avif", "webp"]}
        widths={[400, 600, 800, 1120]}
        sizes="(min-width: 640px) 45vw, 100vw"
        pictureAttributes={{ class: "block h-full w-full" }}
        class="h-full w-full object-cover"
        style="object-position:50% 40%"
      />
    </div>
    <div class="aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden rounded">
      <Picture
        src={beltsAfterTest}
        alt="Newly earned belts tied on after a rank test"
        formats={["avif", "webp"]}
        widths={[400, 600, 800, 1120]}
        sizes="(min-width: 640px) 45vw, 100vw"
        pictureAttributes={{ class: "block h-full w-full" }}
        class="h-full w-full object-cover"
      />
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 md:px-5">
    <div class="pb-14 text-lg leading-loose text-[#40403A] md:pb-16 md:leading-normal">
      <p class="mb-6 md:mb-4">
        Michael's son, {team.headInstructor.name}, runs the school today as head instructor, and
        Michael is still active and involved. {team.headInstructor.name} first stepped onto this mat at
        three years old and has spent twenty-six years in the art since. Same system. Same standard.
      </p>
      <p>
        We have been teaching martial arts since {founded.year}, and most of the people on this floor
        are not strangers. We teach like it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="bg-paper-warm py-20 md:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-6 md:px-5 text-center">
      <p class="mb-5 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-indigo md:mb-3">A Black Belt is not something you simply earn, though you will.</p>
      <p class="mb-5 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-indigo md:mb-3">A Black Belt is not just something you wear, though you will.</p>
      <p class="mb-6 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-indigo">A Black Belt is who you are becoming.</p>
      <div class="text-sm font-bold tracking-[0.08em] text-gold-deep uppercase">{team.founder.honorific} {team.founder.name}, {team.founder.title}</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTASection ctaLabel={offer.cta} ctaHref="/booking">
    <Fragment slot="heading">Come see what's been built <em>since {founded.year}.</em></Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="subtext">Your {offer.first} is on us. No pressure.</Fragment>
  </CTASection>
</BaseLayout>
